# Captured traffic does not live here any more.
#
# It lives outside the repository entirely - see capture-dir.bat, which every
# capture and decode script calls to find it. A capture is a live Anarchy
# Online session from a real account: the login handshake, the account name and
# the credential blob that goes with it, private messages, and every playfield
# the character walked through. That must not reach a public repository, and a
# list of ignore patterns is the wrong thing to rely on to keep it out - it only
# has to be forgotten once, and it was: 81 stream csv files and 27 decoded
# transcripts were tracked here until 2026-09-11.
#
# So the rule is now the stronger one. The data is not in the tree, and cannot
# be committed by accident. The patterns below are a backstop for anything that
# writes into this directory anyway, not the primary defence.

pcap/
*.pcapng
*.pcap
*.marks.txt

# Reassembled streams, decoded output and everything derived from them.
*.csv
*.txt
!n3imp.txt
!client-actions.csv
!client-commands.csv

# Extracted game content. AreaExtract writes the quest text, NPC dialogue and
# object placements of a live playfield out of the traffic. That is Funcom's
# content, lifted verbatim - useful to build against, not ours to redistribute.
# The tool that produces it is in git; what it produces is not.
arete-landing/
extracted-*/
playfields.dat

# Build output. build.bat compiles the tools into bin\ and copies the runtime
# assemblies they need from OmniCell/Built beside them. Rebuild with build.bat.
bin/
*.tmp

# Backstop, in case a binary lands outside bin\ anyway.
*.exe
*.pdb
*.dll
*.exe.config
